  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Criminal Procedure. The vs Unknown on 4 September, 2012 Author: P.Bhavadasan Bench: P.Bhavadasan In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr.Justice P.Bhavadasan Tuesday, The 4Th Day Of September 2012/13Th Bhadra 1934 Bail Appl..No. 6204 of 2012 () ------------------------------ In Crmc.1886/2012 of D.C & Sessions Court,Trivandrum In Cmp.1735/2012 of J.M.F.C.-Iii,Trivandrum In Crime No.732/2012 Of Museum Police Station, Trivandrum. Accused(S)/5Th Accused: ---------------------- Abdul Salam, Aged 42 Years S/O.Abdul Rehman, Charuvilakathu Veedu, Kuruvani Thiruvananthapuram. By Adv. Sri.G.Sudheer Complainant(S): --------------- State Of Kerala Represented By The Public Prosecutor High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam. By Public Prosecutor Smt. Kochumol Koduvath This Bail Application Having Come Up For Admission On 04-09-2012, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: Criminal Procedure. The vs Unknown on 4 September, 2012 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/143958674/ 1 ds P.Bhavadasan,J. --------------------------------- B.A.No.6204 Of 2012 --------------------------------- Dated this the 4th day of September, 2012 Order This is an application for bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.",
    "facts": "Order This is an application for bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. The petitioner is the 5th accused in Crime No.732 of 2012 of Museum Police Station, Thiruvananthapuram, who is alleged to have been committed offence punishable under Sections 273, 328 read with 34 IPC and Section 59(3) of the Food Safety and Standard Act 2006. 2. The allegation is that on 10.7.2012 accused 1 to 4 sold degraded food item known as 'Shavarma' to the defacto complainant and 10 others resulting in the death of one such person due to after effects of consuming food supplied by accused 1 to 4. Allegation against the petitioner is that he had supplied putrified chicken which was cooked and served by hotels. The petitioner was arrested on 19.7.2012 and since then he has been in custody. The petitioner claim that he is totally innocent and he is falsely implicated in the case. At any rate, it is pointed out that his continued custody is unnecessary. 3. The learned Public Prosecutor very vehemently opposed the application and releasing the petitioner now on bail.",
    "arguments": "4. After having heard the learned counsel for the petitioner and the learned Public Prosecutor, it is seen that the only allegation against the petitioner is that he has supplied putrefied chicken which was cooked and supplied to the consumers by the hotels.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "4. After having heard the learned counsel for the petitioner and the learned Public Prosecutor, it is seen that the only allegation against the petitioner is that he has supplied putrefied chicken which was cooked and supplied to the consumers by the hotels.",
